Z||000000||Denny||06-24-2001||02:06 PM||||I need some info . . .<P>My 86 SE V6 auto is idling fast (1200 RPM) in park. Just started doing this. Replaced the IAC with a known good one (throttle body is clean), still doing same thing.<P>The SES light comes on briefly, then goes off.<P>I suspect the EGR tube because nothing happens when I manually compress the diaphragm. My GT stumbles when I do this. The EGR valve works when I apply vacuum.<P>My questions:<BR>1. Is it the EGR tube?<BR>2. Has anyone out there bought anything from IRM recently?<BR>3. If the answer to 2 is yes, how was delivery?<BR>4. If the answer to 2 is "good," when is the best time (or day) to call?<P>With high cost of this sucker, $90 + shipping (includes gaskets) from IRM, $95 + shipping (gaskets extra) from The Fiero Store, I want to make sure it's the problem is the tube, and I'd like to get the IRM one because of the design.<P>***********<P>Forgot to mention that there is no code set.<P>***********<P>Update @ 4:59 PM: Took the tube off, broken at the upper plenum end, also completely clooged with black gunk. Going to try ordering from <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com/," TARGET=_blank>http://www.gmpartsdirect.com/,</A>  PN 10137017, $47.88, can't tell if that includes the gaskets.<P>***********<P>[This message has been edited by Denny (edited 06-24-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Denny (edited 06-24-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000001||FieroJoe||06-24-2001||10:36 PM||||Yes, that is a common high idle fix for V6's...<P>And if you can get the tube brand new at that price, go for it.  If it dosent include the gaskets, I'm sure they arent much extra from the same place too.  Maybe even a local place will have them, and then you wouldnt get dinged on shipping.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
